	(text "INTERNAL 24V LOSS RESET — REV B DRAFT, NOT FOR PRODUCTION\nTPS3808G01DBVR: trip 20.6145V nominal; 20.150…21.081V by prior tolerance calculation.\nR122 gives RESET release delay 180…420ms. This is NOT a purge duration.\nTPS3808 RESET is isolated from DevKit C6: R123=100k pulls U121 input; U121=SN74LVC1G07DBVR.\nU121 is +3V3 powered, open-drain output; R124=680R 1% 0.1W limits C6 discharge current.\nR124 output net DEVKIT_EN_J1_3 connects only to DevKitC-1 V1.1 J1.3 EN (CHIP_PU), NOT GPIO.\nCalculation (not measurement): at 3.0…3.6V, I_U121_peak <=4.456…5.348mA; EN_low <=0.709…0.748V\nusing VOL=0.55V, R5=10k±1%, C6=1uF±10%; VIL_nRST=0.25VDD; t_to_VIL <=2.841ms.\nU121 guaranteed 24mA sink gives K_I>=4.49 (>1.30); R124 peak <=19.2mW, 0.1W gives K_P>=5.20 (>1.25).\nESP32-S3 tRST min=50us; supervisor hold 180ms min. Real waveform/relay dropout/fuel interlock require bench verification.\nLocal nets on this standalone draft do NOT connect to root. No USB power, fuel/glow hardware or purge claim is shown here."
	(at 145 150 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	)
